# Line endings, enforced at checkin.
#
# `.editorconfig` states `end_of_line = lf` and `.prettierrc` formats to it, but neither can
# enforce it: git never reads `.editorconfig`, and prettier only formats files it is pointed
# at — a scripted rewrite, a `sed -i`, or a contributor with `core.autocrlf=true` bypasses
# both. Before this file existed, seven tracked files carried CRLF *in the index*, and the
# LF convention silently broke twice in a single day's work (see issue #84).
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect which files are text and normalize those to LF in the object
# store, leaving each working tree free to check them out however the platform prefers.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text. Git's own heuristic already classifies
# the PNGs under docs/images/ correctly, but stating it means a future asset type cannot be
# guessed wrongly the first time someone commits one.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tgz   binary
